; letters.hasm — every letter opcode, on the real pipeline.
;
; "Satu huruf adalah satu instruksi utuh" was true in the interpreter and
; false in hardware, and nothing said so: no testbench and no program ever
; executed one of the twenty-eight. RTL_IMPLEMENTED listed them, but that set
; is a declaration, not a measurement.
;
; What was wrong was a second `default:` in the middle of the codex result
; case in hcpu_execute.v. Verilog allows one. iverilog resolved it to the
; trailing `default: ;`, so every letter wrote nothing; verilator refused the
; file outright, which is why `python3 rtl/scripts/lint_hcpu.py` had been
; failing. The Python machine has no case statement and kept computing the
; right answer.
;
; Two checks, both against numbers the explicit HLOAD/HCADD path already
; produces:
;   0x100  ||Ba+Sin+Mim||^2   = 112, the same value tb_gowin_top reads
;   0x101  all 28 accumulated, squared norm
        L_BA
        L_SIN
        L_MIM
        HNRM2 R1, H0
        MOVI R5, 0
        STORE R1, R5, 0x100
        L_ALIF
        L_BA
        L_TA
        L_TSA
        L_JIM
        L_HA
        L_KHA
        L_DAL
        L_DZAL
        L_RA
        L_ZAY
        L_SIN
        L_SYIN
        L_SHAD
        L_DHAD
        L_THA
        L_ZHA
        L_AIN
        L_GHAIN
        L_FA
        L_QAF
        L_KAF
        L_LAM
        L_MIM
        L_NUN
        L_WAW
        L_HAA
        L_YA
        HNRM2 R2, H0
        STORE R2, R5, 0x101
        HALT
